From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Barry Pollard <barrypollard@google.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 13:12:55 +0100
Subject: Live Metrics: Handle empty INP entries

Web-vitals v6 can emit INP events without entries for small interactions
after a bfcache restore or a soft navigation (to handle the fact that
those navigations do not have `first-input` events as they will have
been used up on the original hard navigation). See
https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals/issues/724. DevTools
currently expects entries so doesn't handle this well.

This CL adds optional chaining to handle this. The entries aren't needed
for these small interactions as they are only emitted on navigation, and
the log is cleared on navigation so it's safe to clear them.

Bug: 543499029
Change-Id: I36364b9c130db26ef3ca34560214590d9b24e04e
Fixed: 543499029
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/devtools/devtools-frontend/+/8300032
Reviewed-by: Philip Pfaffe <pfaffe@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Barry Pollard <barrypollard@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Victor Porof <victorporof@chromium.org>
